{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789479493,"nonce":"35O9znLhe9y741Bf2/l2CZqvuQs=","title":"Booleans and small integers are boxed to shared static boxes","message":"Every `bool` and every integer in a small range that a program boxes to `Any` gets a fresh pool block, and the data kernels box such values on every step: a record's flags and counters, a token's kind, the result of every comparison stored into a container. bench_records made and released about a million boxes of `True`/`False` and of integers under a hundred, and each one was a pool pop, a header write and a later free.\n\nChange: `zyntax_compiler::interned` holds one static table of boxes, the two booleans then the integers from -5 to 256, laid out like the runtime's `DynamicBox` so a read sees an ordinary box. The boxes pass, when the tiered runtime turns interning on, boxes a `bool` as a select of the two addresses and an `i64` through a range check that splits the block: in range, the address is `base + (v - min) * stride`; out of range, `make_box` as before; the two meet at a phi. A shared box is never released: `zyntax_free` asks `is_interned` only in its not-a-slab branch, since the table is a heap allocation outside the pool's slabs, so a pool block's free (the hot path) pays nothing. The check itself is one subtraction and one compare against the table's base and byte length.\n\nMeasured on the M1 Pro, in-process bench, exec ms: records 350 to 215 (5 collections to 2), tokenize 190 to 118, pipeline 88 to 80. The creation-side branch costs nothing on any_field/any_cast/op_overload_ref (interleaved on/off within noise). A first version put the `is_interned` check at the top of `zyntax_free`, which cost 7% on those three kernels (6.4 to 7.0 ms); moving it under `!in_a_slab` recovered it.\n\n`ZYNTAX_DISABLE_INTERNED_BOXES=1` turns the sharing off; safe to run with, every box is then made fresh.\n\nNot done: strings (`\"\"` and one-character strings) and floats stay fresh boxes; a released box that reaches `zyntax_box_free` through the runtime's droppers goes through the same `zyntax_free` path and is covered.","files":null}]}